NAME
       vgdisplay - show the details of LVM volume groups

SYNOPSIS
       vgdisplay [-s] [-v] [-C] [VG...]

DESCRIPTION
       vgdisplay prints a block of details for each volume group: its name,
       status, number of LVs and PVs, total size, the extent size (PE Size),
       the total number of extents, and how many extents are allocated and
       free (Alloc PE / Size, Free PE / Size). Those last lines are what you
       need before lvcreate -l or lvextend.

OPTIONS
       -s, --short
              One short line per volume group.

       -v, --verbose
              Also show the LVs and PVs of each group.

       -C, --columns
              Print a table like vgs.

EXAMPLES
           vgdisplay vgdata
           vgdisplay vgdata | grep -e 'PE Size' -e Free

SEE ALSO
       vgs(8), pvdisplay(8), lvdisplay(8), vgcreate(8)
